@startuml F02-coupon-status-lifecycle
title F02 — Cycle de vie du statut d'un coupon (vu de l'UI CouponsManager)

[*] --> draft : creation (F01)

state "draft\n(Brouillon)" as draft
state "active\n(Actif)" as active
state "paused\n(En pause)" as paused
state "archived\n(Archive)" as archived

draft --> active : « Activer »\nPOST status {active}
draft --> archived : « Archiver »\nPOST status {archived}

active --> paused : « Pauser »\nPOST status {paused}
active --> archived : « Archiver »\nPOST status {archived}

paused --> active : « Activer »\nPOST status {active}
paused --> archived : « Archiver »\nPOST status {archived}

archived --> archived : transition non-archived\n=> 409 (lock terminal)

note right of archived
  Etat TERMINAL.
  L'UI ne propose plus que « Stats ».
  Toute autre cible cote serveur => 409.
end note

note bottom of active
  Apres chaque POST ok :
  refresh() = GET /api/admin/coupons
  recompose le badge + les boutons.
  Echec (403/409/422/500/network)
  => role=alert, statut inchange.
end note

archived --> [*]
@enduml
